== Real: a browser (Chromium) on http://127.0.0.1:8090
- Signed in with the app password; signed out and in again.
- Setup: typed the owner's npub, chose an option with the keyboard alone (Tab, then arrow keys:
  the focus ring and the chosen card both show), read each option's panel, ticked the
  acknowledgement (Create stays disabled until then), created the community.
- The connecting screen: the status list, then the Cloudflare values with copy buttons.
- Settings, Change the address: the button stays disabled until the current address is typed
  exactly and the box is ticked; the change went through and the page showed the new address.
- Found and fixed on the way: with Referrer-Policy no-referrer, the browser sent the page's own
  forms as Origin: null and the first version refused every sign-in. The page now sends
  same-origin, and checks Sec-Fetch-Site, which doesn't depend on the Host that Umbrel's proxy
  forwards.

